  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "1) Evidence/uncertainty: We have only one completed experiment (config_001: RNA-only, singleprofile, pca_n2000 → 48.5% acc). We have zero information about whether the image modality carries any discriminative signal. This is the most fundamental uncertainty in a multimodal study. 2) What this tests: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) isolates the image modality's contribution under the same singleprofile setting, giving us a clean second unimodal baseline to compare against the RNA-only result. 3) Why it's the best next experiment: Before investing in multimodal fusion configurations (which change modality, add an image encoder, and introduce a fusion strategy simultaneously), we must know whether the image features are informative at all. If image-only performs comparably to RNA-only, multimodal fusion becomes highly promising and we can prioritize those configs next. If image-only is much weaker, we should focus on RNA encoder/aggregation improvements. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the most important design axis (modality contribution) and directly guides the next 2-3 experiments in the budget."
}

